hermes v2026.9.14 (0.21.3): with the Camofox backend the vault tools never
reach the page, so the agent cannot save or fill a login.

Symptom: on any login page (GitHub, IPRoyal, GISTDA) browser_vault_save_login
answers "Open the site's login page first; the login is saved for that page's
origin." and browser_vault_fill answers "Could not determine the current page
origin. Navigate to the login page first."

Cause: the vault reads the page origin, inspects the form and writes the
password through tools/browser_vault_tool.py's _eval_js/_eval_js_secret, which
know only the CDP supervisor and the agent-browser CLI `eval`. Camofox
(Firefox over Juggler) has neither: no supervisor is ever attached, and the
CLI is not installed ("agent-browser CLI not found"), so the origin read fails
and both tools stop there. browser_console works because browser_tool routes
it to Camofox's POST /tabs/<id>/evaluate.

Upstream: NousResearch/hermes-agent#135204 (open) routes the vault's eval
through that same Camofox route; the maintainer keeps it open waiting for a
core seam since Camofox moved out of core into hermes-official-plugins
(#143146). Nothing is merged.

Fix: in Camofox mode, _eval_js and _eval_js_secret evaluate on the task's
Camofox tab through POST /tabs/<id>/evaluate; _focus_bound_origin (CDP tab
focusing) is skipped, the task has one tracked tab. The password travels in
the JSON body of an authenticated request to the agent's own owner-only
server, never in argv; camofox-browser logs only the result's type. Without a
tab nothing is opened; a tab the server closed (404/410) is forgotten so the
next browser_navigate opens a new one. Origin checks (pre-check and the
in-page assert of the fill script) are unchanged.

The new test fails before this change: the origin read goes to the
agent-browser CLI.

